+    # reparent the tee row (12340) to launcher pid 1 instead of buzz 12300, keep owned set
+    # closed by adding the tee's new parent linkage consistently: the closure no longer
+    # reaches 12340 from 12300, so closure would fail too — instead keep closure intact by
+    # moving a SEPARATE extra tee row. The structural rule is: a row naming PINNED_TEE_PATH
+    # must be parented by buzz. Add a FOREIGN tee row parented by pid 1 (not in closure —
+    # exempted by its pinned-path cmd) — then the first 'if not tee_pids' stays satisfied
